  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Belgrade Centre for Security Policy - Human Rights Defenders in Serbia; From Enmity to Partnership</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to strengthen the position and effectiveness of human rights defenders in Serbia by building their capacities, improving the overall environment for their work, and raising public awareness of their importance. It focuses on tailored support, advocacy, and visibility efforts through needs assessments, expert assistance, public events, and awareness-raising campaigns. In the long term, the project seeks to contribute to a safer and more supportive social environment in which human rights defenders can act more effectively and with greater public recognition. In addition to supporting CSOs, the project has a special focus on women activists within CSOs, who are particularly exposed to state pressure, and therefore includes a focus on psychosocial support, especially for women working in CSOs.</narrative>
  </description>
